        "ids": [
          {
            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "2515831"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in JupyterLab. Improper validation of `sideBySideLeftMarginOverride` and `sideBySideRightMarginOverride` settings within the `overrides.json` file allows for cross-site scripting (XSS). An attacker can exploit this by convincing a user to import a specially crafted settings file, or by placing such a file in a shared settings location. Successful exploitation can lead to arbitrary code execution, enabling the attacker to read or modify notebooks and files, and run code through the notebook server.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "jupyterlab: JupyterLab: Cross-site scripting (XSS) allows arbitrary code execution",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "This Important cross-site scripting (XSS) flaw in JupyterLab allows arbitrary code execution when processing a specially crafted overrides.json file. An attacker could either plant a malicious settings file in a shared location, leading to automatic execution, or trick a user into importing one. This grants the attacker the ability to read/modify user files and execute code with the user's permissions, impacting Red Hat OpenShift AI and Migration Toolkit for Applications deployments.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
        ],
